{"title":"2025 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Michael, Nico, and Jackson are splitting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill. Michael's favorite number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> so he insists on paying a positive amount of dollars that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Nico and Jackson are both scared of even numbers, so they each insist on paying an odd number of dollars. In how many ways can they pay the bill?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d859e4443415bc115f926374648de5f694305d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" /> In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fdfbb0362c49460ab4b7ef61acc59d3b0fac79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a right angle. If the median from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/74489604477e43bae4b6e6ec28436a306982f5ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> find the maximum possible area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d859e4443415bc115f926374648de5f694305d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" /> The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are written on a board. Every second, if the numbers currently on the board are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1d002db36c51a77f8fbc6314e96756fc793e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> is written, and one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is erased. After a finite number of seconds, the larger number on the board is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b44aa28bf84afb8038174179eb1e6bfb01d709c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\sqrt{T}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"34\" />. How many possible values can the smaller number take?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018070714\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 82/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3143/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33838:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018070714 and revision id 260083. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}